        "Line.40.Third.Image": "'He separates himself from his associates' – (because) he cannot help (the ruler).",
        "Line.40.Fourth.Statement": "He separates himself from his associates. There will be good fortune.",
        "Line.40.Fourth.Image": "'He separates himself from his associates' – (because) he cannot help (the ruler).",
        "Line.40.Fifth.Statement": "He rightly obtains the praise (due to him), and in his dwelling-place there is good fortune. He has obtained the (right) position, and is free from anxiety.",
