        "Line.46.Fourth.Image": "'He separates himself from his associates' – (because) he cannot help (the ruler).",
        "Line.46.Fifth.Statement": "He rightly obtains the praise (due to him), and in his dwelling-place there is good fortune. He has obtained the (right) position, and is free from anxiety.",
        "Line.46.Fifth.Image": "'He rightly obtains the praise (due to him)' – (because) he is in the central position, and is correct.",
        "Line.46.Sixth.Statement": "He has (the happiness of) a (simple) cottage. He puts aside his (ornamental) vessels. He keeps his person retired and unknown, but maintains his principles and acts in accordance with them.",
