        "Line.33.First.Statement": "You guard your jaws and are still. Good fortune.",
        "Line.33.First.Image": "'You guard your jaws and are still' - because one knows to be content with little.",
        "Line.33.Second.Statement": "You guard your jaws and are still. Misfortune.",
        "Line.33.Second.Image": "'You guard your jaws and are still' - because one retreats from the proper path.",
        "Line.33.Third.Statement": "You guard your jaws but are not still. Misfortune.",
        "Line.33.Third.Image": "'You guard your jaws but are not still' - because one loses proper conduct.",
        "Line.33.Fourth.Statement": "You guard your jaws. Good fortune. The dripping nourishes.",
        "Line.33.Fourth.Image": "'You guard your jaws' - because one is in proper position. 'The dripping nourishes' - because it brings brilliance.",
        "Line.33.Fifth.Statement": "You retreat from guarding your jaws. Good fortune.",
        "Line.33.Fifth.Image": "'You retreat from guarding your jaws' - because one is supported by central position.",
        "Line.33.Sixth.Statement": "You guard your jaws and are still. Misfortune.",
        "Line.33.Sixth.Image": "'You guard your jaws and are still' - because one is at the top and without support.",
        "Line.53.First.Statement": "Establish order within the family. Regret disappears.",
        "Line.53.First.Image": "'Establish order within the family' - because one's will is directed toward correcting relationships.",
        "Line.53.Second.Statement": "There is no need to go outside the family. Persistence brings good fortune.",
        "Line.53.Second.Image": "'There is no need to go outside the family' - because the proper focus is on household matters.",
        "Line.53.Third.Statement": "When family members are severe, there will be regret and danger. But if there is harmony and discipline, good fortune.",
        "Line.53.Third.Image": "'When family members are severe' - because the position is not central, requiring balance.",
        "Line.53.Fourth.Statement": "Enrich the family. Great good fortune.",
        "Line.53.Fourth.Image": "'Enrich the family' - because harmony makes relationships prosperous.",
        "Line.53.Fifth.Statement": "The king approaches his family. Do not worry. Good fortune.",
        "Line.53.Fifth.Image": "'The king approaches his family' - because love and harmony bring mutual affection.",
        "Line.53.Sixth.Statement": "Be sincere and trustworthy. Good fortune in the end.",
        "Line.53.Sixth.Image": "'Be sincere and trustworthy' - because this principle establishes order throughout family.",
        "Line.54.First.Statement": "Advancing and retreating. Perseverance of a military man will be advantageous.",
        "Line.54.First.Image": "'Advancing and retreating' - because the will is in doubt. 'Perseverance of a military man' - because the will is set on bringing order.",
        "Line.54.Second.Statement": "Gentleness under the bed. Employing shamans and wizards in multitudes. Good fortune, no blame.",
        "Line.54.Second.Image": "'The good fortune of employing multitudes of shamans and wizards' - because he has obtained the middle course.",
        "Line.54.Third.Statement": "Repeated gentleness. Humiliation.",
        "Line.54.Third.Image": "The humiliation of 'repeated gentleness' - because the will is exhausted.",
        "Line.54.Fourth.Statement": "Remorse disappears. Taking the field, three kinds of game are obtained.",
        "Line.54.Fourth.Image": "'Taking the field and getting three kinds of game' - because he has done what is right.",
        "Line.54.Fifth.Statement": "Perseverance brings good fortune. Remorse disappears. No disadvantage. Being at first without constant, but at last with constant. First for three days, then for three days. Good fortune.",
        "Line.54.Fifth.Image": "'Perseverance brings good fortune and remorse disappears' - because he is in the central and correct position.",
        "Line.54.Sixth.Statement": "Gentleness under the bed. Losing his property and axe. Perseverance will be evil.",
        "Line.54.Sixth.Image": "'Gentleness under the bed' - because he is at the top and exhausted. 'Losing his property and axe' - though correct, it is evil.",
        "Line.27.First.Statement": "He meets with his mate. They are both of the same character. There will be no blame.",
        "Line.27.First.Image": "'He meets with his mate' – (because) corresponding (elements) are moved together.",
        "Line.27.Second.Statement": "He meets his equal. There will be good fortune.",
        "Line.27.Second.Image": "'He meets his equal' – (because) he is in the central position.",
        "Line.27.Third.Statement": "He separates himself from his associates. There will be no blame.",
        "Line.27.Third.Image": "'He separates himself from his associates' – (because) he cannot help (the ruler).",
        "Line.27.Fourth.Statement": "He separates himself from his associates. There will be good fortune.",
        "Line.27.Fourth.Image": "'He separates himself from his associates' – (because) he cannot help (the ruler).",
        "Line.27.Fifth.Statement": "He rightly obtains the praise (due to him), and in his dwelling-place there is good fortune. He has obtained the (right) position, and is free from anxiety.",
        "Line.27.Fifth.Image": "'He rightly obtains the praise (due to him)' – (because) he is in the central position, and is correct.",
